Your sword lashes out again and opens a second cut across Bram's shoulder, and the dead thing rocks but stays up. This time its answering swing gets through — a heavy fist catches you across the helm and jaw, and your head rings, the taste of iron in your mouth. The thing presses in, its lantern light swinging wild against the drift walls.

You're on your feet, shield up, and Bram is torn and sagging before you, still shambling, still holding its light. Behind you Ged keeps his lamps high, and you can hear his ragged breathing.

What do you do?


